.TH KKFETCH 1 "September 2026" "kkfetch 0.15.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kkfetch \- A fast, lightweight Linux system information fetch tool written in Rust
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kkfetch
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kkfetch
is a high-performance system information tool designed for speed and aesthetic terminal output.
It gathers hardware and software details with minimal latency.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-modules\fR \fI<MODULES>\fR
Enable specific modules in order (comma-separated, e.g. "os,kernel,cpu,memory").
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-disable\fR \fI<DISABLE>\fR
Disable specific modules (comma-separated, e.g. "gpu,disk").
.TP
\fB\-\-no-color\fR
Disable colored ANSI output.
.TP
\fB\-\-no-plugins\fR
Disable execution of external shell plugins.
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-logo\fR \fI<LOGO>\fR
Override the ASCII logo (e.g. "arch", "debian", "ubuntu", "ferris", "fedora", "tux").
.TP
\fB\-\-no-logo\fR
Do not display any ASCII logo.
.TP
\fB\-\-list-modules\fR
List all available information modules and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-disk-path\fR \fI<DISK_PATH>\fR
Target mount point or directory path for disk usage statistics (default: "/").
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output system information in structured JSON format.
.TP
\fB\-\-timings\fR
Show execution latency breakdown per module in microseconds.
.TP
\fB\-\-doctor\fR
Check system environment for multiple or conflicting kkfetch installations.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help information.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version information and check for conflicting installations.
